    "https://jobs.careerbeacon.com/details/department-of-psychology--tenure-track-assistant-professor-in-developmental-psychology/2239456": {
      "title": "Department of Psychology: Tenure Track Assistant Professor in Developmental Psychology",
      "description": "Department of Psychology:  Tenure Track Assistant Professor in Developmental Psychology at University of New Brunswick (Academic) | Careerbeacon.com University of New Brunswick (Academic) Department of Psychology:  Tenure Track Assistant Professor in Developmental Psychology Saint John, NB Apply Later Apply Now Discover The Opportunity Saint John, NB In-person Education and Training Experienced Full-time Competition Number: 26-04 The Department of Psychology at the University of New Brunswick in Saint John, N.B., invites applications for a tenure track position in Developmental Psychology at the rank of Assistant Professor, commencing July 1, 2027, subject to final budgetary approval. The University of New Brunswick respectfully acknowledges that its Saint John campus sits on unsurrendered and unceded traditional Wolastoqey land. The lands of Wabanaki people were recognized in a series of Peace and Friendship Treaties to establish an ongoing relationship of peace, friendship and mutual respect between equal nations. The river that runs by our university is known as Wolastoq, along which live Wolastoqiyik, \"the people of the beautiful and bountiful river.\" Wolastoq is also known as the St. John River. Candidates must have a Ph.D. in Psychology or a related field, specializing in Developmental Psychology. Specific areas of interest can be broad within this field, but experience and expertise in neuropsychological or neuroscientific methods is required, as the successful candidate will contribute to newly launched graduate programs in Neuroscience (including a traditional MSc and PhD, and a course-based Masters in Applied Neuroscience). The successful candidate will teach a range of courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels, which will include Child Development, Adulthood and Aging, and other Developmental Psychology courses. They will also contribute to other teaching in the Department of Psychology at the undergraduate and graduate level. The successful candidate will be required to develop an original research program, including the supervision of undergraduate and graduate students. Evidence of research and teaching competence will be required, as indicated by the submission of a statement of research interests and experience, a teaching dossier, teaching evaluations, and reference letters from individuals familiar with the candidate's teaching and research capabilities. The Department of Psychology on the Saint John Campus of UNB offers undergraduate programs in Psychology and Biology-Psychology, as well as a thesis-based Master of Arts in Psychology, a course-based Master of Applied Psychology, Research, and Evaluation, and a Ph.D. in Psychology that is offered jointly with the Department of Psychology at UNB Fredericton. From Fall of 2027 the Department will also offer graduate programs in Neuroscience. The Department has a strong background in experimental/applied psychology and solid links with Horizon Health Network, Dalhousie Medicine New Brunswick, the provincial government, and non-profit organizations supporting the community. Faculty in the Department also contribute to the Ph.D. in Clinical Psychology Program offered at UNB Fredericton. Review of applications will begin on October 31, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Applicants should submit their application package by clicking on the \"apply now\" button above. The package should include: (1) cover letter describing educational background and research expertise, relevant experience, and future research goals, (2) their CV, and other files, including (3) a statement of research interests, (4) a statement explaining how you integrate Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion into your academic work, (5) a teaching portfolio including a statement of teaching philosophy, and (6) up to three reprints of recent publications. Academic references will be requested from all short-listed candidates. Questions can be directed to Dr. Jonathan Wilbiks, Chair of the Department of Psychology ( [email protected] ). The salary for the position depends on the rank at which the successful candidate is hired. Faculty salary grids by rank are available here: https://www.unb.ca/hr/_assets/documents/salary-grids.pdf. Salary and fringe benefits are governed by Sections 35 and 36B of the Association of University of New Brunswick Teachers (AUNBT) 2025-2029 Collective Agreement. Applicants should clearly state whether they are a Canadian citizen, a permanent resident of Canada, or an international applicant. All shortlisted candidates will be expected to provide confirmation of credentials, including appropriately certified translations of credentials into English, as applicable. The University of New Brunswick is committed to employment equity and fostering diversity within our community and developing an inclusive workplace that reflects the richness of the broader community that we serve. The University welcomes and encourages applications from all qualified individuals who will help us achieve our goals, including women, visible minorities, Aboriginal persons, persons with disabilities, persons of any sexual orientation, gender identity or gender expression. Preference will be given to Canadian citizens and permanent residents of Canada. Look for yourself Photo Gallery A little bit about us University of New Brunswick (Academic) The University of New Brunswick employs more than 3,200 full- and part-time staff, including faculty, support staff and students. UNB values people and we have proudly been named as one of Canada\\'s Top 100 Employers for 2026 and one of Atlantic Canada\\'s Top Employers for 2026. UNB is situated on the unceded territory of the Wolastoqiyik and Mi\\'kmaq peoples along the banks of the beautiful and bountiful Wolastoq river, a region recognized worldwide for its natural beauty. UNB is a comprehensive university with a long history of excellence in teaching and research. Apply Now View Careers Page Powered by Apply Later Enter your email to receive a reminder to apply for this position at a later date. * Email Apply Later We will send you an email reminder to with a link to this job. Cancel Create Reminder"
